Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 10:42:28 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 23/35] feat: film halation - red-orange halo around
 emulsion-overloading sources (bloom domain)

New HDRHalation post-effect param container (HDR_Halation_Amount/Threshold/Radius/Tint), r_HDRHalation cvar (2 = diagnostic force), and a bloom-stage pass: threshold with a high knee (a bright sky must not halate), a wide separable spread through the streak stretch shader (the engine's gaussian utility is pinned to +-8 texels), two narrow gaussian passes to round the tap gaps into a soft edge, and a tinted additive composite with the same bloom-weight compensation as the streaks plus an 8x gain so the halo reads at the strength an overloaded frame really shows. Component group Halation (amount, threshold, radius, tint) pushed verbatim - a film-stock property, so it does not follow the f-number. Reviewed by the main session; user verification pending.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017nykaDjTHxHDSo11CsYx6M
